message: "If you use these results or the method, please cite this repository."
title: "Six open unit-fraction questions answered with machine-checked certificates: Erdős #307 (coprime variant), odd Znám, odd Giuga, Brenton–Hill n₀ = 2, and Borwein et al. Problems 7 and 8"
authors:
  - family-names: Phillips
    given-names: Doug
date-released: 2026-11-25
version: 1.0.0
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - Znám's problem
  - Erdős problem 307
  - Egyptian fractions
  - unit fractions
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
abstract: >-
  An explicit solution of Znám's problem consisting of 24 odd integers, and a solution of the coprime,
  1-excluded variant of Erdős Problem #307, both found by a residue-steered implicit descent and verified in
  Lean 4 (kernel-checked, standard axioms only). Developed with AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic; see README).
